--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/add-kolla-ansible-image-0746f6311029c37f.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+---
+features:
+  - |
+    Adds a ``kolla-ansible`` image, which packages Kolla-Ansible as a
+    deployment tool. The image contains Kolla-Ansible, a supported version
+    of ``ansible-core``, and every Ansible collection Kolla-Ansible needs,
+    all installed at build time into ``/usr/share/ansible/collections``,
+    so that nothing is fetched from Ansible Galaxy or git when the image
+    runs. Its entrypoint is ``kolla-ansible``, so
+    ``docker run kolla-ansible --help`` works without any wrapper.
+    The image records the Kolla-Ansible version, the git commit of each
+    source tree it was built from where known, and the installed
+    collections in ``/etc/kolla-ansible/deployer.json``. Kolla-Ansible is
+    taken from the ``kolla-ansible`` source and the ``openstack.kolla``
+    collection from the ``kolla-ansible-plugin-ansible-collection-kolla``
+    source, both of which can be overridden in ``kolla-build.conf`` to
+    build the image from local or patched trees.
